id: pm-graph-main-ci-coverage
title: Restore main CI after evidence-path coverage falls below the exact floor
description: "Main run 40788717831 and release PR 183 runs fail at the exact LCOV line threshold: 99.6965% is below 99.7%, although the native report rounds it to 99.70%. All parent tests pass; the intentional nested fixture failure is expected. Add deterministic coverage for the new validator witness branches and make nested fixture diagnostics unambiguous without changing thresholds."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags[3]: ci,coverage,regression
created_at: "2026-10-30T13:54:27.237Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-30T17:23:26.780Z"
author: codex-agent
resolution: Add deterministic real no-git witness coverage and clearer nested-runner diagnostics; enforce uncached measurement. Full npm and Bun gates pass 453 tests each at unchanged thresholds. Preserve the documented historical reproduction limit.
comments[13]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-30T13:54:30.750Z",codex-agent,"Full job logs inspected for main Node 26 job 123168292149 and release PR 183 Node 22/26 jobs 123507257346 and 123507256951. Every parent test passes; assertThresholds rejects exact 99.6965% lines against 99.7%. Newly introduced scripts/validate-evidence-path.ts lines 48-50 (cheaper and longer witnesses) are uncovered. Reproduce the unchanged CI release command first, then cover deterministic real no-git tracker scenarios and label expected fixture diagnostics."
  "2026-10-30T13:57:25.866Z",codex-agent,"The existing validator test uses the same tracker after 500 mutation sequences, so its graph does not guarantee a cheaper longer path. Add an independent five-item tracker with explicit relationships and costs implied by sorted IDs, asserting all 25 queries, 13 reachable proofs, and exactly one cheaper/longer witness. Run without git on PATH and verify source bytes remain unchanged."
  "2026-10-30T14:06:41.850Z",codex-agent,"Focused disposable-worktree suite passed 25/25, zero skips/TODOs/cancellations. Behavioral revert proof: restoring only original runCoverageGate makes the new captured-output regression fail (1/1) because intentional child failure output corrupts the parent receipt. Fixed implementation restored in finally; diagnostic and exact 99.6965%-versus-99.7% precision regressions then pass 2/2. No coverage floor or source exemption changed."
  "2026-10-30T14:21:05.498Z",codex-agent,"Additional disposable-worktree mutation proof: disabling only the validator cheaper/longer witness counters makes the deterministic tracker regression fail (actual 0 versus expected 1). Restored original validator in finally; regression passes 1/1 afterward. This demonstrates behavioral protection of the uncovered branch, independent of aggregate coverage arithmetic. CI extension installation and strict project health also pass; one pre-existing stale-item advisory remains."
  "2026-10-30T14:34:34.794Z",codex-agent,"The unchanged local Node 26.13 baseline completed successfully: 450/450, 99.77% native lines, while validate-evidence-path still misses lines 48-50. Compared with all three failing CI logs, Node 26.13 reports five additional covered lines in the defensive impact-envelope branch (src/index.ts 3690-3694). Starting one unchanged baseline on the CI Node 26.12 line to verify this runtime-dependent coverage difference. The fix guarantees validator witness coverage rather than relying on incidental engine accounting."
  "2026-10-30T14:37:50.338Z",codex-agent,"Target-worktree linked acceptance executed through pinned pm test --run --only-index 1 --progress under Node 26.12: 25/25 passed, no failures/skips/TODOs/cancellations. TypeScript test build passes. Public evidence scan found no absolute local paths in the new item/history, regression file or root-cause documentation."
  "2026-10-30T15:12:59.553Z",codex-agent,"Correction: the unchanged Node 26.12 baseline also passes 450/450 at 99.77%, so runtime version alone does not explain local versus CI counts. Node documents reduced V8 coverage precision with compile caching; the pinned CLI enables that cache programmatically. A real warmed-module probe changes branch coverage from 66.67% with caching disabled to 50.00% with it enabled. Add an unconditional NODE_DISABLE_COMPILE_CACHE guard to measured child processes, with a real regression asserting both inherited caches and module API activation are disabled. Then compare an unchanged cache-disabled baseline before the fixed full gates."
  "2026-10-30T15:20:29.325Z",codex-agent,"Cache guard regression now passes against a genuinely warmed module, and verifies a later native enableCompileCache call returns DISABLED. Reverting only the guard makes that regression fail; restored in finally and cache/diagnostic cases pass 2/2. The final linked focused suite passes 26/26 with zero skips/TODOs/cancellations. Starting the unchanged full release command with compile caching disabled to compare precise cold-cache counts against the CI failure."
  "2026-10-30T15:47:31.343Z",codex-agent,"The current-main cache-disabled control also passes at 99.77%, so cache effects are not established as the cause of the five extra local line hits. Retain cache disabling for Node-documented measurement precision and its independently passing regression. Earlier controls used current main SDK 2026.10.26 and Node 26.12.0/26.13, whereas failed b790904 pins SDK 2026.10.25 and CI used Node 26.12.1. Installed that exact commit lockfile in a separate disposable worktree and verified the official Node 26.12.1 archive checksum. The original full release command is now running against those exact inputs with CI identity settings and credential-free child environment."
  "2026-10-30T16:23:20.956Z",codex-agent,"Full-log phase correction: main Node 26 job first passed npm release:check (450 tests, 99.77% lines), then failed the following Bun release gate at exact 99.6965%. Earlier npm controls therefore reproduced the passing half. Host Bun 1.3.5 also passes, while the failing job installed Bun 1.4.4. Verified the official Bun 1.4.4 release asset digest and am now running the complete original CI setup and sequential npm/Bun gates on b790904, locked SDK 2026.10.25, Node 26.12.1 and Bun 1.4.4, sharing one fresh CI home and isolated compile-cache directory."
  "2026-10-30T16:51:51.747Z",codex-agent,"Exact-tuple local result: b790904 with its original lockfile, Node 26.12.1 and Bun 1.4.4, project extension install and sequential npm/Bun gates in one fresh CI environment passes 450/450 at 99.77% lines in both phases. The historical aggregate failure is not reproduced locally; do not claim otherwise. All controls still leave validator lines 48-50 uncovered. Historical logs establish the 99.6965% failing profile, and the deterministic real-tracker test explicitly covers the missing behavior. Full patched gates are now running on current main pins at unchanged thresholds; disclose the reproduction limit in the PR and final handoff."
  "2026-10-30T17:06:07.813Z",codex-agent,"Patched npm release:check passes every phase with 453/453 tests and zero failures/skips/TODOs/cancellations. Exact LCOV: 33 runtime sources, lines 7238/7257 = 99.7381838%, branches 2691/2812 = 95.6970128%, functions 517/517 = 100%. Validator is now 78/78 lines. With its three witness-counting lines uncovered, this measured profile would be 99.6968444%, below the unchanged 99.7% floor. This is a calculated counterfactual, not a claimed historical whole-suite reproduction. Bun 1.4.4 full gate is running next; dist and dependency pins remain unchanged."
  "2026-10-30T17:23:24.381Z",codex-agent,"Both complete patched release gates pass with Node 26.12.1 and Bun 1.4.4: npm 453/453 (lines 99.7381838%, branches 95.6970128%, functions 100%); Bun 453/453 (lines 99.8070828%, branches 95.7977208%, functions 100%). Each reports all 33 runtime modules with zero failures, skips, cancellations or TODOs. Typecheck, lint, duplication, build, docstrings, audit, pack, changelog and publication-policy checks all pass. Validator coverage is 78/78 lines; dist rebuild and dependency pins have no diff. Diagnostic/cache/witness mutation proofs fail when reverted and pass after restoration. Historical full-run failure remains unreproduced locally and is explicitly documented. Implementation complete; claim released for orchestrator verification. PR branch CI will provide final-head verification."
